//@version=6
indicator("UCTPROBE_SYMINFO", overlay = false)

// ⭐⭐ THE NINE `syminfo.*` FIELDS THIS ENGINE REFUSES BY NAME, asked of the
// vendor in one sitting. `symbolScope.json::unserved` is the roster and every
// entry there carries a REASON — this probe exists because several of those
// reasons are about OUR side of the wire, and the owner's standing criterion is
// identity with TradingView. A reason not to GUESS is not a reason not to
// MEASURE.
//
// ⛔⛔ READ THE ROSTER'S REASONS BEFORE READING THE RESULT, because they are not
// all the same kind of reason and the result does not settle all of them:
//
//   basecurrency  "answering it for an equity would mean choosing between
//                  `USD` and the empty string, and a script that branches on
//                  that branches on our guess."          ← MEASUREMENT settles it
//   timezone      "holds no session calendar"            ← MEASUREMENT settles it
//                                                           IF the answer is a
//                                                           constant for our
//                                                           whole universe
//   type,         "constant across everything this engine holds, so serving it
//   currency       would let a multi-currency script look like it was working
//                  while one whole branch was unreachable."
//                                                        ← a UX objection, NOT a
//                                                           parity one. Under
//                                                           identity-with-vendor
//                                                           a constant that
//                                                           MATCHES is correct.
//   mintick,      "differs per symbol and is not something this engine holds"
//   pointvalue                                           ← settled only if the
//                                                           witnesses AGREE
//   root          "a futures concept … equities have no expiry to strip"
//                                                        ← MEASUREMENT settles it
//   session       "no session calendar per symbol"       ← same as timezone
//
// ⛔ `description` IS DELIBERATELY NOT ASKED. Its refusal is the one reason a
// vendor reading cannot touch: it is free text *from a data vendor*, it differs
// between OUR providers for the same symbol, and a script branching on it would
// branch on which provider answered. TradingView having one answer does not give
// US one. Asking would produce a number that looks like progress and unblocks
// nothing (`lesson_an_audit_is_where_to_look_not_what_to_trust`).
//
// ⛔ A FAILED STUDY KEEPS A ONE-PLOT STUB with an EMPTY `_data._items`, so a
// capture that reads the roster without first asserting `isFailed === false`
// records a study that never evaluated as though it had answered. See
// `exchange-spelling.pine`, which learned that from a `syminfo.exchange` that
// does not exist in Pine v6.

// ── STRINGS: equality in the member's own operator ──────────────────────────
// ⭐ EQUALITY, NOT CONTAINMENT, for the reason `exchange-spelling.pine` gives at
// length: a member's script writes `syminfo.currency == "USD"`, so the probe has
// to ask in that operator. Containment answers a weaker question and is exactly
// how a whitelist "looks correct on this one example".

// S1-S2 — basecurrency. THE TWO CANDIDATES THE ROSTER NAMES, asked directly, so
// the answer is not inferred from a length that both could share.
plot(syminfo.basecurrency == "USD" ? 1 : 0, "S1_base_eq_USD")
plot(syminfo.basecurrency == ""    ? 1 : 0, "S2_base_eq_EMPTY")
// S3 — and its length, so a THIRD answer nobody predicted arrives as a lead
// rather than as two zeros. (`exchange-spelling.pine` N10's rule.)
plot(str.length(syminfo.basecurrency), "S3_len_base")

// S4-S5 — currency. Expected "USD" for every symbol this engine can reach; a
// disagreement here is more interesting than an agreement.
plot(syminfo.currency == "USD" ? 1 : 0, "S4_curr_eq_USD")
plot(str.length(syminfo.currency), "S5_len_curr")

// S6-S8 — type. The roster says it is constant across our universe; that is a
// claim about US equities, and these three ask whether the vendor agrees on the
// spelling as well as the constancy.
plot(syminfo.type == "stock"  ? 1 : 0, "S6_type_eq_stock")
plot(syminfo.type == "equity" ? 1 : 0, "S7_type_eq_equity")
plot(str.length(syminfo.type), "S8_len_type")

// S9-S12 — timezone. The three spellings a US-equity chart plausibly returns.
// ⚠️ "Exchange" is included because Pine accepts it as a TIMEZONE ARGUMENT
// elsewhere, so it is a real candidate spelling rather than a guess.
plot(syminfo.timezone == "America/New_York" ? 1 : 0, "S9_tz_eq_NY")
plot(syminfo.timezone == "Etc/UTC"          ? 1 : 0, "S10_tz_eq_UTC")
plot(syminfo.timezone == "Exchange"         ? 1 : 0, "S11_tz_eq_Exchange")
plot(str.length(syminfo.timezone), "S12_len_tz")

// S13-S14 — root. The roster rules it a futures concept; the only question is
// what an EQUITY returns. ⭐ ASKED AGAINST `syminfo.ticker` RATHER THAN A
// LITERAL, so one probe answers it for every witness symbol at once.
plot(syminfo.root == syminfo.ticker ? 1 : 0, "S13_root_eq_ticker")
plot(str.length(syminfo.root), "S14_len_root")

// S15-S16 — session. If this is one constant string across every witness, the
// roster's "no session calendar" objection stops being a parity blocker for the
// universe this engine actually reaches.
plot(syminfo.session == "regular" ? 1 : 0, "S15_sess_eq_regular")
plot(str.length(syminfo.session), "S16_len_sess")

// ── NUMBERS: read directly, because they need no candidate set ──────────────
// ⭐⭐ THESE TWO ARE THE EASY HALF AND THE ROSTER'S REASON FOR THEM IS THE ONE
// A SINGLE SYMBOL CANNOT SETTLE: "differs per symbol". A number plots itself, so
// the question is not what ONE symbol says, it is whether the WITNESSES AGREE.
// ⛔ Do not conclude from one row.
plot(syminfo.mintick, "S17_mintick")
plot(syminfo.pointvalue, "S18_pointvalue")

// ⛔ S19 IS THE NON-VACUITY CONTROL AND IT IS NOT OPTIONAL. Every equality above
// can legitimately read 0 and `str.length` can legitimately read 0 for an empty
// string — so "this symbol matched nothing" and "the study never evaluated" are
// otherwise the SAME ROW OF ZEROS, and a capture that cannot tell those apart is
// not evidence. `syminfo.ticker` is served today and is never empty, so a 0 here
// means the probe is broken and the whole row must be discarded.
plot(str.length(syminfo.ticker), "S19_len_ticker_CONTROL")

// ── how to run it ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ⛔ FOLLOW `docs/pine/capture-procedure.md` — never add a study while the tab is
// hidden, and restore symbol, resolution, pane stretch factors and study
// visibility afterwards. The browser is shared with other sessions.
//
// ⭐ THIS IS A VALUE CAPTURE, so it survives a hidden tab once the study is on
// the chart: read `study._data._items`. ADDING the study still needs a visible tab.
//
// WITNESSES — ⛔ MORE THAN ONE, AND THAT IS THE POINT FOR S17/S18. The string
// fields are expected to be constant across US equities; the numbers are not.
//
//     SPY     an ETF on NYSE Arca — the flagship divergence in the sibling probe
//     AAPL    an ordinary NASDAQ equity
//     BRK.B   a dual-class share, where the ticker itself carries a dot
//     F       a sub-$20 name, in case mintick tiers below some price
//
// ⭐ AND ONE NON-EQUITY, WHICH IS WHAT MAKES S1/S2 READABLE. `basecurrency` is
// defined as the left half of a pair, so a symbol that HAS two currencies is the
// control proving the field is populated at all:
//
//     BITSTAMP:BTCUSD    expect basecurrency "BTC", currency "USD"
//
// ⛔ WITHOUT THAT ROW, `basecurrency == ""` on an equity is ambiguous between
// "the vendor returns empty for equities" and "this probe cannot read the field".
// The crypto row discriminates them, and it is the only row that can.
//
// RECORDING — the same four fields every `confirmed` entry needs:
// `{pine, witness, captured, how}`. An entry without a witness is an assertion
// wearing a data structure.
//
//     "_invocation": "tools/visual_conformance/probes/syminfo-roster.pine pasted
//                     into the TradingView editor; plot values read from
//                     study._data._items per docs/pine/capture-procedure.md"
